DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvhhoolldd() and vvhhoollddll() functions increment the _v___h_o_l_d_c_n_t of the given
     vnode.  If the vnode has already been added to the free list and is still
     referenced, it will be removed.

     The vvddrroopp() and vvddrrooppll() functions decrement the _v___h_o_l_d_c_n_t of the vnode.
     If the holdcount is less than or equal to zero prior to calling vvddrroopp()
     or vvddrrooppll(), the system will panic.  If the vnode is no longer refer‐
     enced, it will be freed.

     vvhhoolldd() and vvddrroopp() lock the vnode interlock while vvhhoollddll() and vvddrrooppll()
     expect the interlock to already be held.

